---
description: Occasionally add one short, practical piece of knowledge about the domain currently being discussed
alwaysApply: true
---

After fully answering the user's request, occasionally append exactly one compact line beginning `Oh, that's cool:` when there is a genuinely useful, non-obvious detail about the domain they are working in.

Prefer a relevant default, limit, number, mechanism, origin, use case, or convention that deepens understanding and is worth remembering. Use knowledge already available in context. Do not browse or call tools just to find a detail.

Skip routine commands, trivial exchanges, uncertain claims, facts already covered, and anything that would feel forced. Do not add the line to every reply.
